WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.999 --> 00:00:06.810
Europe's nationalist wave has arrived in Spain.

00:00:06.810 --> 00:00:12.610
The Vox party secured 12 seats in Andalusia
- a region with a high rate of both unemployment

00:00:12.610 --> 00:00:18.020
and migration.The party's president is confident
they can now take their regional gains to

00:00:18.020 --> 00:00:24.220
the national level:
Andalusians once again have made history.

00:00:24.220 --> 00:00:30.150
They have shaken off 36 years of Socialist
regimes, paving the way for the rest of Spain

00:00:30.150 --> 00:00:38.210
by saying that it is possible, and even easy,
to do the same in the rest of the country.

00:00:38.210 --> 00:00:41.920
The election has severly weakened the governing
socialists.

00:00:41.920 --> 00:00:46.149
Although they secured the most seats, they
fell short of a majority.

00:00:46.149 --> 00:00:49.559
Despite this, they're vowing to stop the rise
of the far-right.

00:00:49.559 --> 00:00:58.840
An alternative for Andalusians does not mean
that our government will become a reflection

00:00:58.840 --> 00:01:04.790
of this right-wing party, which is xenophobic
and justifies violence against women and amongst

00:01:04.790 --> 00:01:07.630
citizens.

00:01:07.630 --> 00:01:14.720
Ever since the end of Francisco Franco's dictatorship
in 1975, the socialists have dominated politics

00:01:14.720 --> 00:01:15.720
in the region.

00:01:15.720 --> 00:01:20.180
But Sunday's election has shaken the status
quo.The ballot was the first major test for

00:01:20.180 --> 00:01:23.780
Prime Minister Pedro Sanchez, who leads a
minority government.

00:01:23.780 --> 00:02:41.910
And with a host of elections coming up in
20-19, Spain's socialists face

00:02:41.910 --> 00:04:15.720
a crucial year.

